{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:98598",
  "title": "Critical: freerdp security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-13 12:06:37"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-24 06:08:10"
  },
  "severity": "Critical",
  "description": "FreeRDP is a free implementation of the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP), released under the Apache license. The xfreerdp client can connect to RDP servers such as Microsoft Windows machines, xrdp, and VirtualBox.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* FreeRDP: freerdp-proxy: FreeRDP: Information disclosure via uninitialized heap memory in Save Session Info PDU (CVE-2026-85089)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Arbitrary code execution via oversized channel messages in SHOW_PROTOCOL (CVE-2026-91948)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via crafted Surface Bits command (CVE-2026-91954)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Remote code execution via heap buffer overflow in Server Redirection PDU (CVE-2026-91964)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Information Disclosure via RDPGFX ResetGraphics PDU (CVE-2026-91946)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP 3.0.0 through 3.30.0 Protocol Negotiation Bypass (CVE-2026-91949)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds read in URBDRC channel (CVE-2026-91956)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via out-of-bounds write in urbdrc client channel (CVE-2026-91951)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Remote code execution via uninitialized heap memory disclosure (CVE-2026-91963)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Use-after-free vulnerability in DRDYNVC parser leads to memory corruption (CVE-2026-91947)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service due to buffer over-read in RPC gateway (CVE-2026-91959)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Out-of-bounds read leads to denial of service or information disclosure (CVE-2026-91950)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via integer overflow and double free in WinPR (CVE-2026-91960)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Heap buffer overflow via oversized LB_LOAD_BALANCE_INFO routing token can lead to heap corruption. (CVE-2026-91953)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP: Denial of Service due to out-of-bounds read in smartcard response processing (CVE-2026-91945)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via uninitialized progressive tile handling (CVE-2026-109242)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP 3.0.0-beta1 before 3.32.0 Use-After-Free via Smartcard Connect (CVE-2026-109676)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Unauthenticated keystroke injection via premature input dispatch (CVE-2026-110838)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via file descriptor exhaustion in serial device handling (CVE-2026-110830)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap-based buffer overflow during MP3 audio decoding (CVE-2026-110837)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via unbounded memory consumption during RDPDR reassembly (CVE-2026-110833)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via grayscale JPEG clipboard conversion (CVE-2026-110839)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via memory exhaustion in NLA frame parser (CVE-2026-111378)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Arbitrary code execution via crafted persistent cache file (CVE-2026-111379)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Arbitrary code execution via crafted persistent cache file (CVE-2026-111381)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Arbitrary code execution via crafted display frames (CVE-2026-111382)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap out-of-bounds write in NTLM authentication (CVE-2026-111880)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: heap buffer overflow in server rdpsnd via crafted audio formats (CVE-2026-114045)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via malformed image clipboard payloads (CVE-2026-121386)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via zero-width graphics reset (CVE-2026-121402)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via zero-length dynamic virtual channel messages (CVE-2026-121404)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via uncontrolled memory allocation in dynamic virtual channels (CVE-2026-121388)\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via assertion failure in RemoteFX decoder (CVE-2026-121394)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Rebase FreeRDP to 3.32.2 or newer [rhel-10.3.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-277443)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
